bof-o2	hello world\nsecond line\nthird\n	0	-	-	-	o2	a digit with no selection, and nothing to do with `meow-block` any more. This buffer holds no brackets at all, so `o` finds no block in Emacs either and the two agree about it; what is left is the digit, which Meow then refuses for the reason recorded against `bof-b2`.
